            {
                "entry_id": "bc9d7676-4130-356a-9eda-037d9d6ba456",
                "word": "ka",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f38971a8-68d2-4589-92b4-c92a48d0990f",
                        "entry_id": "bc9d7676-4130-356a-9eda-037d9d6ba456",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "kâ"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5740e848-f0af-33a8-ac9b-46409d4ea2e5",
                        "entry_id": "bc9d7676-4130-356a-9eda-037d9d6ba456",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Le double, une des parties de l’âme humaine."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Mythologie égyptienne"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "08438791-b82d-4436-9354-ffcb4f5055e4",
                                "sense_id": "5740e848-f0af-33a8-ac9b-46409d4ea2e5",
                                "text": "À côté du corps il y a ce que J. Vandier appelle « les principes spirituels » (5): akh, ba, ka, khaibit, ren, śẖm (6). On est d’autant plus puissant, semble-t-il, que les âmes sont nombreuses ; et on peut même, à cet effet, avoir plusieurs âmes de la même catégorie. L’akh, force divine attribuée originellement aux dieux et au roi qui leur est assimilé, fut très tôt accordée à tous les hommes. Le ba, représenté par un oiseau (cigogne ?) de même que l’akh (ibis), et traduit en général […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "44f9995e-7a33-4ad9-a834-1c73292a437a",
                                "sense_id": "5740e848-f0af-33a8-ac9b-46409d4ea2e5",
                                "text": "Que ton ka te protège et te garde en longue vie, dit l’autre."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0c0324d5-e1dc-4e1b-872e-759dd7db73fd",
                        "source_entry_id": "bc9d7676-4130-356a-9eda-037d9d6ba456",
                        "source_sense_id": "5740e848-f0af-33a8-ac9b-46409d4ea2e5",
                        "target_lang_word": "ka",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ka",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "835b7315-1f5b-35ce-8da9-379438eb6380",
                                        "entry_id": "cd149612-6631-3a61-a440-500cabf56f78",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A spiritual part of the soul in Egyptian mythology, which survived after death."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4714676c-7903-4c5a-b970-8601881bbfd4",
                                                "sense_id": "835b7315-1f5b-35ce-8da9-379438eb6380",
                                                "text": "Then, I wondered how long I must wait before seeing my Double, but if I recalled, the Ka was not supposed to appear before the seventy days of embalming were done."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c44a8b69-dd03-4060-8e3a-93b8ad91dc85",
                                                "sense_id": "835b7315-1f5b-35ce-8da9-379438eb6380",
                                                "text": "Hence Dorian's portrait is like the ka or double of the deceased in Egyptian tombs, heaped with toys and furniture."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c34f0cdc-698c-45fb-9865-ea0fccfada8f",
                                                "sense_id": "835b7315-1f5b-35ce-8da9-379438eb6380",
                                                "text": "‘You could bind the ka of a man to his body for five thousand years,’ said Jaquel."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "ka",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "88b33126-bbe8-3425-adb3-e2024c5f43b3",
                                        "entry_id": "e61f11cd-db75-39c0-b67e-2b9b5b8cd6bc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To serve or help; used only in the phrase \\\"Ka me, ka thee\\\" or variants thereof."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "064aa575-20f8-4551-a264-ea84789a379a",
                                                "sense_id": "88b33126-bbe8-3425-adb3-e2024c5f43b3",
                                                "text": "Now nature stood ever on this point, Kæ mee Ile kæ thee, and ever ready to bee even alwaies on recompences and vicissitude of things, and to give as good as one brings."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ae07c84-fe7f-422e-ab5d-9ac39d059c42",
                                                "sense_id": "88b33126-bbe8-3425-adb3-e2024c5f43b3",
                                                "text": "Ka me, ka thee, is a proverb all over the world."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "ka",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fcdbcd7e-46e3-3ad6-bfb9-60722e9cb0c2",
                                        "entry_id": "ecb643e8-d6fd-3a39-a791-0db337c0412f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The name of the Cyrillic script letter К / к."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
